clude/boost/asio/detail/reactive_wait_op.hpp:84\n#18 0x529ef0 in boost::asio::detail::scheduler_operation::complete(void*, boost::system::error_code const\u0026, unsigned int) /usr/include/boost/asio/detail/scheduler_operation.hpp:40\n#19 0x529ef0 in boost::asio::detail::scheduler::do_run_one(boost::asio::detail::conditionally_enabled_mutex::scoped_lock\u0026, boost::asio::detail::scheduler_thread_info\u0026, boost::system::error_code const\u0026) /usr/include/boost/asio/detail/impl/scheduler.ipp:486\n#20 0x529ef0 in boost::asio::detail::scheduler::run(boost::system::error_code\u0026) /usr/include/boost/asio/detail/impl/scheduler.ipp:204\n#21 0x529ef0 in boost::asio::io_context::run() /usr/include/boost/asio/impl/io_context.ipp:63\n#22 0x529ef0 in eventloop::EventLoop::startEventLoop() ../git/sd_event_loop.cpp:245\n#23 0x4e1190 in main ../git/main.cpp:120\n#24 0x75b2f76c  (/lib/libc.so.6+0x2176c)\n#25 0x75b2f86c in __libc_start_main (/lib/libc.so.6+0x2186c)\nAddress 0x7eaf1630 is located in stack of thread T0\nAddress 0x7eaf1628 is located in stack of thread T0\nSUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: memcpy-param-overlap (/usr/lib/libasan.so.6+0x33074) in __interceptor_memcpy\n\u003d\u003d1283\u003d\u003dABORTING\n\nASan reports the following overlapping ranges:\n\n[0x7eaf1630, 0x7eaf163f)\n[0x7eaf1628, 0x7eaf1637)\n\nBoth addresses are on the stack.\n\nIn the original implementation, retval points to either ipv4addr or ipv6addr, and the std::string conversion happens at return retval;. Although the arrays are still alive at that point, ASan is detecting an overlapping source/destination during the string construction.\n\nI moved the buffers outside the if/else-if blocks, and with that change the ASan memcpy-param-overlap report no longer occurs in my testing.\n\nSo my original assumption that this was caused by the scope/lifetime of the arrays was not accurate. The change was intended to address the stack overlap observed by ASan, rather than a dangling-pointer issue.",
